agent/src/agent/context-size.ts:6:// prompt of that single call in three parts: input_tokens (uncached), cache_read_input_tokens, and
agent/src/agent/context-size.ts:7:// cache_creation_input_tokens. Their sum is the full prompt the model read for this decision,
agent/src/agent/context-size.ts:8:// including the part served from the prompt cache and the provider's own tool-use preamble, which
agent/src/agent/context-size.ts:9:// the provider counts but does not show. This is a per-call value, not a run or billing total.
agent/src/agent/context-size.ts:10:// We record it as "measured", with the cached share kept separately.
agent/src/agent/context-size.ts:11://
agent/src/agent/context-size.ts:12:// If the response carries no usage (stream cut off, aborted call), we fall back to the
agent/src/agent/context-size.ts:13:// count_tokens estimate taken just before the call for the same request, and mark it "estimated".
agent/src/agent/context-size.ts:14:// If neither exists the value is null with status "unavailable". It is never reported as 0.
agent/src/agent/context-size.ts:15://
agent/src/agent/context-size.ts:16:// This harness never compacts, summarizes, or truncates history inside a run, so compacted is
agent/src/agent/context-size.ts:17:// always false; a run that would outgrow its token budget stops instead (see budget.ts).
